USC: precision of 8-bit integer test masks

On vec34 cores GenerateInt8Comparison makes its TESTMASK with an 8-bit ALU
(ISUB8/ISUBU8) and a precision mask, but ConvertTESTToUseasm only gave the
32 and 16-bit ALUs their precision flag, so any comparison of char or uchar
failed to assemble ("For a isub8 instruction with test and the .msk flag
either .i8 or .i10 flags must be present").  The 8-bit ALUs get .i8.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/asm.c b/tools/intern/usc2/asm.c
index faed7a1..f8aee07 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/asm.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/asm.c
@@ -5300,6 +5300,16 @@ static IMG_VOID ConvertTESTToUseasm(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE psState, PINST psIn, PUS
 					psOut->uFlags2 |= USEASM_OPFLAGS2_MOVC_FMTI16;
 					break;
 				}
+
+				case USEASM_OP_IADD8:
+				case USEASM_OP_IADDU8:
+				case USEASM_OP_ISUB8:
+				case USEASM_OP_ISUBU8:
+				{
+					/* A byte per channel (GenerateInt8Comparison). */
+					psOut->uFlags1 |= USEASM_OPFLAGS1_MOVC_FMTI8;
+					break;
+				}
 	
 				default: 
 				{
